        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अतिथी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अतिथी — atithī — \"an honoured guest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "समारंभाला मोठे अतिथी आले होते. samārambhālā moṭhe atithī āle hote. Distinguished guests had come to the ceremony."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "More formal than पाहुणा; the plural is the same: एक अतिथी (atithī), अनेक अतिथी (atithī)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अतिथी (atithī) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit atithi, \"a guest\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
